            </section>
            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 84-year-old male patient, admitted on 25/10/2005 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, physical examination revealed reduced air entry bilaterally with expiratory wheezing. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation consistent with COPD. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. Pulse oximetry demonstrated oxygen saturations of 84% on room air. The patient was treated with nebulized bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and intravenous fluids. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He was discharged in stable condition with optimized inhaler regimen and oral steroid taper. Please arrange early follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
